Table-by-Table Explanation
1. users — Customers
sql
id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
Field	Purpose
id	Auto-generated UUID (no need to manually assign)
email	Unique — no duplicate customer accounts
created_at	Tracking when the customer signed up
Used by: Subscription (Java) to create accounts, marks the root entity of the system.

2. plans — Product Catalog (Pricing)
sql
id UUID PRIMARY KEY,
name TEXT NOT NULL,              -- e.g., "Basic", "Pro", "Enterprise"
price_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,     -- ints, never floats! (avoids rounding errors)
currency TEXT DEFAULT 'USD',
interval TEXT CHECK (interval IN ('monthly','yearly'))
Field	Significance
price_cents	Money stored as cents (integer) — crucial for financial accuracy
interval	CHECK constraint enforces only valid billing cycles
Used by: Subscription (Java) references plans for plan selection/upgrades.

Why cents? Floats cause precision issues (0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004). Storing $10 as 1000 cents avoids this entirely.

3. subscriptions — The Lifecycle Table
sql
id UUID PRIMARY KEY,
user_id UUID REFERENCES users(id),
plan_id UUID REFERENCES plans(id),
status TEXT DEFAULT 'active',
current_period_start TIMESTAMP,
current_period_end TIMESTAMP,
cancel_at_period_end BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
Field	Purpose
user_id → users	Who owns this subscription (FK)
plan_id → plans	Which plan they're on (FK)
status	active (or cancelled/expired — though not constrained here)
current_period_start/end	Billing cycle boundaries (e.g., July 1 → Aug 1)
cancel_at_period_end	Graceful cancellation — keep access until end of cycle, then cancel
Most important table — it's managed by the Subscription Service (Java):

POST /subscriptions → creates a row with status='active'
PATCH .../upgrade → changes plan_id
POST .../{id}/cancel → sets cancel_at_period_end=true
4. invoices — Bills Produced
sql
id UUID PRIMARY KEY,
user_id UUID REFERENCES users(id),
subscription_id UUID REFERENCES subscriptions(id),
amount_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,
currency TEXT DEFAULT 'USD',
status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending',
due_date TIMESTAMP,
created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
Field	Purpose
user_id	Who is billed
subscription_id	Which subscription generated this bill
amount_cents	The total due
status	pending → (later)paid/failed (constrained by the Billing Service)
due_date	Payment deadline
Used by: Billing Service (Python) creates these (POST /invoices/generate), which the Payment Service (Go) settles.

